 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A **queue** belongs to one entity. Attributes:
+
+- `name`, `slug` (unique within the entity).
+- `is_active` flag (default `true`); inactive queues reject issuance.
+- Optional `labels_i18n` (JSON, locale fallback for display names).
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (filled when called). Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
-- Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Display `code`, unique per `(queue_id, code)`.
+- Priority (numeric, see below; `>= 0`, higher = more priority, default `0`).
+- Issuance timestamp `issued_at` (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` (default), `printed`.
+- Status: `waiting` (initial) → `called` (no cancelled status).
+- Call fields `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (nullable, set once at call time).
+
+### Display code
+
+Per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, … (prefix `A`, at least 3 digits, zero-padded; beyond 999 it grows: `A1000`, `A1001`, …). The next code is "last valid code + 1" by insertion order (not string order, so `A999` then `A1000` yields `A1001`); deleting a ticket does not reuse its number. Malformed legacy codes (anything not matching `A<digits>`) are skipped.
+
+### Issuance (`App\Actions\IssueTicket`)
+
+- New tickets are `waiting`, `issued_at = now()`, default channel `virtual`, default priority `0`. Negative priority is rejected (`InvalidArgumentException`).
+- Inactive queues are rejected (`App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException`, nothing persisted). The queue row is re-read and locked inside the transaction, so a queue deactivated after the caller loaded it is still rejected.
+- Concurrent issuance retries a few times on a unique `(queue_id, code)` collision.
+
+### Write-once
+
+After issuance every ticket field is immutable except `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` (and `updated_at`). Any Eloquent save/update changing another field throws `LogicException`.
+
+### Single call (`Ticket::call(User $user)`)
+
+A ticket can be called exactly once: it becomes `called` with `called_at` and the calling user recorded. Only members of the ticket's entity may call (others: `AuthorizationException`, ticket unchanged). Calling a non-`waiting` ticket throws `LogicException`. Selection of *which* ticket to call next (priority/fairness) is out of scope.
 
